  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Anaesthetic Record completeness engine. calculateGrade returns status ('incomplete' if any of the 8 critical mandatory rules is unsatisfied, else 'partial' if any of the 4 non-critical rules is, else 'complete'), completenessPercent = round(100 x satisfied / 12), firedRules (all 12 rules in catalogue order, each with satisfied true/false - so the array is always 12 long), criticalMissing and noncriticalMissing. Flags are SPLIT: form-app.js calls detectFlaggedIssues(state, grade) with the whole grader result, mirrored here as flagsArgs ['state','result']; the oracle stores them under expected.flaggedIssues. Quirks verified in source: M-WHO-CHECKLIST is satisfied by ANY non-empty whoSignIn/whoTimeOut (so 'no' counts as recorded) while F-WHO-CHECKLIST-001 fires whenever either is not exactly 'yes'; consentConfirmed '' or 'no' both raise F-UNLOGGED-CONSENT-001; the allergy conflict is a case-insensitive substring match of each >=3-char allergy term (split on , ; / newline and the word 'and') INSIDE the drug name, so a class allergy ('penicillin') is missed for a drug whose name does not contain the term (co-amoxiclav) but caught for benzylpenicillin; derangement uses strict < 92 / < 90 (exactly 92 and 90 are normal) and counts observation ROWS not breaches; the priority sort is stable so within a priority the flags keep detection order (WHO, allergy, airway, anaphylaxis, consent). Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas anaesthetic-record --update",
